<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:07.110
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:07.110 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.360
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:27.100
<i>Sir Guin's rushed plans to launching the Willgem...</i>

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.110
<i>...incited an attack from Dianna Counter.</i>

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:32.400
<i>And so, we found ourselves under attack by five WaDoms.</i>

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:39.120
<i>During this, I discovered yet more of White Doll's fighting power.</i>

00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:44.040
<i>However, at the same time, Keith's criticism put a heavy burden on me...</i>

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:47.830
<i>...And I seem to have lost my place in Milady Sochie's heart.</i>

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:57.090
<b>The Battle Of Enlightenment</b>

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.020
I really can walk on my own.

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:17.110
I imagine you don't often get the chance to walk this far, Lady.

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:18.240
But...

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:21.120
Ooh, I can smell Heaven!

00:02:21.410 --> 00:02:23.700
Give it a whiff!

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:25.870
Is that...

00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:34.500
- It sounds like a flute.
- A flute?

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.720
Sounds like a small child is playing it.

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:42.930
Shall we go have a look?

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.140
Let's go!

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.900
This shows we weren't completely prepared when we launched it.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.240
That may be, but we had no choice.

00:03:01.610 --> 00:03:02.700
Ahh, they made it here.

00:03:04.910 --> 00:03:06.700
Please watch where you step!

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:08.200
Our friends sure did a number on this one.

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:10.620
The landing's as bad as a crash!

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.210
Can I ask you to be as expedient as possible with the repair?

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.000
The condition of our spaceship...

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:19.010
...will be a pivotal factor in regards to our negotiations with Dianna Counter.

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.220
Just bear in mind that we aren't exactly magicians here.

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.140
- Consider yourself lucky to be alive.

00:03:24.010 --> 00:03:28.720
- Frankly, it doesn't matter how many people we have if they keep fighting us like that.

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:25.930
- Well, excuse me.

00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:32.810
Well, passion and drive motivate us even when our weapons aren't up to par. Willpower does wonders.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:35.110
What?

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:38.230
It's the way you're talking... That sounds like something Gavane would say.

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.610
Is that bad?

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.610
Well, we're fighting against the technology of the moonrace, so we need make use of our wits!

00:03:43.700 --> 00:03:44.820
Our wits?

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:45.530
Right, Loran?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.040
Loran!

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:52.000
You're finished already?

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:56.710
Yes?

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:00.710
Would it be alright if we request the assistance of your female Master?

00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.430
I'm sorry, Miss Kihel isn't with us at the moment.

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:07.430
Oh, doesn't she realize how important our work current is? How careless...

00:04:07.430 --> 00:04:08.720
She's right.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.930
Well, The Lady has a lot of things to think about...

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:12.230
Liar!

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:15.690
You and my sister both don't have any idea how stupid you've been acting.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.900
These days, I simply don't understand what Milady Sochie is thinking either...

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:23.740
What? You actually didn't know, Loran?

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:26.530
Know what?

00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:29.030
I can't believe you're the only one who doesn't get it...

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:39.210
Hey, you don't need to worry about disinfecting a tiny wound like this.

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.840
We're on the earth, not the moon.

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:43.300
It would be a terrible problem if some foreign bacteria snuck in there.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:44.630
Bacteria?

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:46.800
I wish this planet wasn't so damn primitive...

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.140
Give me your hand.

00:04:49.510 --> 00:04:50.720
Have the unit...

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.520
...begin preparations for carrying out the next attack...

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.230
As of now, we've been too badly beaten to do anything yet.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.520
Well, we can't ignore this current situation!

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.530
Perhaps we could ask the Royal Guard to back us up?

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.400
The Royal Guard...

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.700
Poe... is that mouth of yours clean!?

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.620
What's that? This Borjarnon isn't functioning properly?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.620
Mechanical Dolls can be rather difficult, can't they?

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.500
How's it doing?

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:26.510
It's fine. There's a bunch of little nicks in the armor, but a little fighting spirit makes battle damage intimidating!

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.220
Yep, fighting spirit does that!

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.010
What's wrong?

00:05:30.010 --> 00:05:33.100
It's nothing. So, will you be moving to the Willgem after this?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.100
No.

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.600
We've all been recalled to a new location.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.820
They've discovered a new excavation site.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:43.900
With a bit of luck...

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:47.110
It could be a new Mountain Cycle.

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.200
In that case, I'll go with you.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.620
No, you should stay here.

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:59.630
I'd be devastated if by bride's cute little face got badly scarred.

00:05:59.630 --> 00:06:01.840
This isn't any big deal.

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:03.710
No, you gotta take it seriously.

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:04.710
Gavane?

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:12.300
Is it alright for us to leave the Willgem like this?

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:15.020
This Gallop's current mission is to search for Miss Kihel.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.100
Are you sure that's okay? Aren't we in the middle of a war?

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.020
After such a large scale battle...

00:06:20.020 --> 00:06:22.310
The enemy's mobile suits will be in need of repairs.

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:27.320
Furthermore, Milady Kihel Heim is one of Sir Guin Rhineford's most important supporters.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:29.410
- Supporter?
- I thought she was just a secretary.

00:06:29.410 --> 00:06:32.620
Either way. Finding the Lady is my first priority.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.120
Right, right.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.830
But in either case, where have you gone off too, Queen Dianna?

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.500
If she had gone to the Soleil, Lieutenant Harry would have told me...

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:46.920
Not to mention we need to switch and retrieve the true Lady Kihel.

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.430
Make sure you don't wash this off before the ceremony.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.320
- Hurry up or we'll be late!
- I'm going as quickly as I can!

00:07:13.030 --> 00:07:17.540
We don't have time to waste around here! Can't we go?

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:21.420
Time to waste? We can't leave yet.

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:26.210
I've got to make something that proves we were here in this great place!

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:31.430
If I don't do this now, I might not be able to leave a trace of our existence.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.010
I suppose so.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:38.600
At some point sooner or later, many people die and end up forgotten.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.600
No one remembers them, or ever speaks of them.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.940
Do you like this?
- Sure.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:44.940
You can have it.

00:07:44.940 --> 00:07:46.230
Thank you!

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:48.530
That's my mother!

00:07:48.530 --> 00:07:50.530
- She looks weird!
- It's kinda funny!

00:07:50.530 --> 00:07:53.410
What's that?

00:07:54.030 --> 00:07:56.410
- She looks weird!
- Yeah, weird!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:00.700
Kids like you tend to take their own wonderful mothers for granted.

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:05.630
Corin!

00:08:06.840 --> 00:08:10.210
Lookie! She's laughing!

00:08:11.510 --> 00:08:13.930
You're right, I suppose she is.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.640
As I've said, we've located a new mountain out in this direction.

00:08:18.640 --> 00:08:22.600
The ground's texture and composition indicates that it could be a new Mountain Cycle.

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.610
Do you think we'll be able to find any new weapons buried there?

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:28.020
Most likely.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.900
It looks like the Zenoa Team's great efforts have paid off.

00:08:30.900 --> 00:08:33.030
We've detected radiation there.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.820
Could radioactive ore be in there?

00:08:34.820 --> 00:08:38.830
You should be able to use some of the mobile suit forces to speed up the excavation.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.200
I intended to ask you for permission to do so, Thank you very much.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:48.920
If we can gain hold of the fire power inside this Mountain Cycle, it could give us the edge we need.

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:51.000
Commander Phil's Mobile suits...

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.920
What is it?

00:08:53.510 --> 00:08:57.220
It appears that we've located the woman who resembles Queen Dianna.

00:09:00.720 --> 00:09:02.220
What is the meaning of this?

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:03.930
Impossible!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.230
That man is still alive...

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:11.400
...and it seems that Queen Dianna's look-a-like is now with him!?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:12.900
What do you want to do?

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:14.820
We'll need that double.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:17.410
Why does it have to be him, of all people...

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:22.830
Thank you so much! They're even nice enough to feed us!

00:09:22.830 --> 00:09:24.540
Isn't that right, your Majesty?

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:26.420
Yep, it's true.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:31.710
Thank you kindly, great Sun, great Moon!

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.510
Well then, here you go.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.920
Thanks for the food!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.230
Delicious!

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.110
Go ahead and try some, Madame!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:55.400
Sure.

00:09:59.410 --> 00:10:02.410
What's with all of these trees?

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.330
Perhaps if I tried to search for human life signs using the infrared...

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.500
This heat source reads as four or five people...

00:10:18.220 --> 00:10:19.640
Just some cows...

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.430
Where is the festival?

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:23.930
Over by the river!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.600
Alright, let's go!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:27.430
You really don't have to carry him.

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:29.600
- Let's go!
- Let's go!

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:31.100
Your Majesty, Let's Go!

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:33.110
But we're...

00:10:33.110 --> 00:10:35.610
Don't worry about it.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:37.900
Surely, you must both be here for the festival...

00:10:37.900 --> 00:10:39.530
No, we're...

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:41.820
Try this. It's very sweet.

00:10:41.820 --> 00:10:43.120
Sure.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:46.830
It's delicious!

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.410
- Then, go ahead.
- Alright!

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:55.420
Is this one of your father?

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.800
Well, I'll have to think about what my father looked like.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:10:59.010
Is that so?

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:01.220
So, this one should be my father, then?

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:03.430
Here they come!

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:16.530
Is this a celebration of the earth's harvest season?

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.530
Looks kinda crappy if you ask me...

00:11:18.530 --> 00:11:20.610
Well, they're only a poor small village.

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:23.030
Either way, It does remind me of life on the Moon.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.030
I love festivals.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.200
- This stuff's great!
- Yeah.

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.710
Let's get going.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:34.840
Could one of the people in this crowd possibly be Queen Dianna?

00:11:34.840 --> 00:11:36.630
That looks tasty as well!

00:11:39.720 --> 00:11:42.010
A Mobile Suit?

00:11:42.010 --> 00:11:43.220
A Mobile Rib?

00:11:43.220 --> 00:11:44.640
What is it doing here?

00:11:56.730 --> 00:11:57.820
Pardon me!

00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.530
What is this thing?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:03.740
It's a dummy replica of Laura's Mustached Doll.

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.820
Aren't you from the Moonrace?

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.120
They let us join the festival, so we decided to give them a hand!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.330
So the Moonrace and the Terrans are celebrating together?

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.830
A man named Mr. Laijie was a huge help when it came to organizing this event!

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:17.210
It was great.

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:18.710
Keith Laijie...

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:20.420
He did.. all this?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:23.630
You'll just get in their way if you run over there!

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.510
George!

00:12:25.510 --> 00:12:26.930
Queen Diann...

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.930
Milady Kihel!

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.600
Loran, what are you doing here?

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.940
What do you mean? I'm here because I've been searching for you!

00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:53.830
Don't you want to go off with everyone else?

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:55.830
I can see everything from here.

00:12:55.830 --> 00:12:57.250
Oh, I see.

00:12:57.250 --> 00:13:00.250
A spot like this resembles the stairway that a man uses to climb his way up to Heaven!

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.260
Up to Heaven?

00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:05.930
Yeah. There's tasty food here and everything.

00:13:07.930 --> 00:13:10.060
I get it!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:14.520
We must have seen festivals like this one from the moon! That's why we decided to land here!

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.520
Uncle, Uncle!

00:13:17.520 --> 00:13:20.650
Uncle, would you like to stay here with us?

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:22.150
That'd be great!

00:13:35.250 --> 00:13:36.250
Uncle...?

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:55.350
Uncle...

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:01.820
I can't believe the Moonrace and Terrans are actually holding a celebration together!

00:14:01.820 --> 00:14:03.150
It's incredible!

00:14:03.150 --> 00:14:05.240
I too, am amazed by it.

00:14:05.240 --> 00:14:10.030
I heard that our people and the moonrace are together like this because of Keith Laijie!

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.740
Hey, good to see you!

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:14.830
Yeah!

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:19.330
Queen Dianna, do you really think the world will end up like this in the future?

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:22.250
All of these problems occurred due to my absence.

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:25.340
As I continually sorted through our preparations, I let the military handle other matters.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:29.220
I'm sorry, I never meant that you were the one to blame. I just want something good to come from all this.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.850
I'm not sure how I'll be able to resolve this. That's why I intend to return to the moon.

00:14:33.850 --> 00:14:38.940
Without the Soleil, how could you possibly return to the moon?

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:43.440
I can use the Zacktraeger in orbit above the Earth's equator.

00:14:43.440 --> 00:14:45.320
Zacktraeger?

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:48.820
That's correct. It should be the only other route that's left between the earth and the moon.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.660
I haven't heard of it.

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.950
Right. Up until now, that route has been closed off...

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:57.750
But as far as I could tell, it has apparently been opened once again.

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.340
GUNDAM!

00:15:06.340 --> 00:15:07.420
Uh oh...

00:15:10.130 --> 00:15:11.220
Uncle!

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.140
Why does this keep happening...

00:15:15.140 --> 00:15:17.430
That man has returned here to destroy our lives...

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.520
It's Sergeant Corin!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:23.650
I have to destroy you!

00:15:31.660 --> 00:15:33.030
You can't get away from me!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.950
A Mobile Suit!

00:15:38.240 --> 00:15:39.450
Just you watch!

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:40.830
Uncle!

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.750
Don't get close to it! Allow me to take care of him!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.750
Uncle...

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:47.750
- Who the...
- That man is!

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:53.130
That bastard who destroyed heaven has come here! Get out of here, your Majesty!

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.140
I saw him when we were working at Keith's baking factory...

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.720
He's Corin Nander.

00:15:57.720 --> 00:15:58.930
Corin?

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:02.350
Don't you remember? You fought against his Mobile Suit in that underground cavern.

00:16:02.350 --> 00:16:05.650
Right. He was the one who kept shouting that the White Doll was a "Gundam".

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:10.530
Heaven's...!

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:12.150
Please wait, Corin!

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:16.120
You have to stop him!

00:16:16.120 --> 00:16:17.240
Right!

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:19.740
Run! It's dangerous!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:22.330
- What the!?
- A mechanical doll!?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.750
GUNDAM!

00:16:25.250 --> 00:16:26.920
Mr. Corin, please come down from there!

00:16:36.720 --> 00:16:37.640
Run!

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:45.730
You have to stop this! You can't destroy the festival's floats!

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.730
Who the hell are you!?

00:16:47.730 --> 00:16:51.030
You're only going to get yourself hurt if you get between me and that Gundam!

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:55.030
This one isn't the real Gundam. It's a paper mache replica!

00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.240
I have to fight and destroy the Gundam!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.330
Look, it's only made out of paper! See? Paper!

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.620
I'LL WRECK THAT DAMN THING!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:10.630
What the!?

00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:19.220
Sergeant Corin Nander, You clearly don't have any idea what you're talking about!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.720
Harry, lead that person outside the village!

00:17:21.720 --> 00:17:23.140
Yes Ma'am! Roger that!

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.230
The Gold type?

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.320
Loran, We'll let him destroy that fake White Doll.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:39.450
I'm going to need your assistance, Mr. Braun John.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:41.120
You mean that fake White Doll...

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:42.830
...Is the reason for this riot.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.330
Then let's move it away from the festival.
- Okay.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.840
You're saying that we should let him do whatever he wants!?

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.050
That man views this festival as his Heaven.

00:17:57.050 --> 00:17:59.220
Isn't there some way you can help us?

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:01.720
I understand your feelings, but...

00:18:04.430 --> 00:18:06.940
I have no intention of letting that thing harass others!

00:18:06.940 --> 00:18:07.940
Corin!

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.030
Welcome back...

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:27.120
Bruno! Jacop!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:28.540
Sergeant...

00:18:28.540 --> 00:18:31.130
I'm so happy!

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:40.550
What do you intend to do? Are we going to slug it out with that maniac here?

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:47.930
Okay then, let's go...

00:18:48.350 --> 00:18:50.650
...and beat up that blasted Gundam!

00:18:55.650 --> 00:18:57.820
Now what are we supposed to do?

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:03.240
W...w...what!?

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.620
Alright, let's do this!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.620
GUNDAM!

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:10.750
I'll kick your ass!

00:19:11.420 --> 00:19:14.750
Queen Dianna, what should I do!?

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.930
Sorry about this, Loran...

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:23.340
We're far too afraid of that man to disobey him.

00:19:27.930 --> 00:19:28.930
Taste this!

00:19:31.230 --> 00:19:32.730
You can't escape!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.620
BASTARD!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.420
Sheesh, Now what!?

00:19:59.130 --> 00:20:00.630
Here I come, little Miss!

00:20:04.140 --> 00:20:05.140
Mr. Corin!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:09.850
Sergeant!

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.230
Okay, get lost!

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:20.940
Mr. Jacop!

00:20:25.320 --> 00:20:26.530
I've got you!

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.450
Lieutenant Harry!

00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:41.420
Loran, they brought me up to speed. It's best to simply let Corin do as he wishes!

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.930
You must be kidding... How are we supposed to do that?

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.430
By using this!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.350
lt's time to bring this to its conclusion...

00:20:57.860 --> 00:20:59.730
...WHITE GUNDAM!

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:04.650
Please, rest in hell.

00:21:26.430 --> 00:21:27.720
Gundam...

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:32.850
I couldn't just let you do what you wanted, even if everyone else has forgotten.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:41.150
Memories of you still reside in my head. After all, you were the great white devil.

00:21:42.940 --> 00:21:44.940
Is that...true?

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.120
You're leaving?

00:21:49.820 --> 00:21:52.120
Where did the young lady go?

00:21:52.120 --> 00:21:55.330
The princess has been set free from the hateful spirit...

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:59.330
...and so she's finally departed to play in heaven!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:01.920
Are you leaving?

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:11.140
To the great Heaven's Stairway... For Heaven's magnificent bagworm...

00:22:12.060 --> 00:22:16.640
For the sake of calling everyone's soul...

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:21.230
- Wow, I can't stop myself! 
- We should live here!

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:41.190
<i>Lost Mountain.</i>

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:46.440
<i>The mountain that was closed off to everyone...has now been broken into by Dianna Counter and the Suicide Squad.</i>

00:23:47.320 --> 00:23:50.110
<i>They breached it in search of new weapons...</i>

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:54.490
<i>...But, what they find instead is the bitter truth of the Dark History.</i>

00:23:54.490 --> 00:23:56.450
<i>And Milady Sochie cries out in terror.</i>

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:02.250
<i>Next time... on TURN A GUNDAM...
"Sunrise At Midnight"</i>

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:05.460
The God of Death's light has no wind.

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Sunrise At Midnight</b>
